# Conventions UX Trajectoire

## États Async Obligatoires
Tout composant qui fetch des données expose ces 4 états :
```typescript
type AsyncState<T> =
  | { status: "idle" }
  | { status: "loading" }
  | { status: "success"; data: T }
  | { status: "error"; message: string };
```

## Hiérarchie Server / Client
```
Page (Server Component)         → fetch initial data, auth guard, redirect
  └── [Name]Client.tsx (Client) → état local, interactions, events
        └── [Name]Panel.tsx     → sous-composants purs si possible
```

`"use client"` uniquement si :
- Hooks navigateur (MediaRecorder, Speech API)
- État local interactif (useState, useReducer)
- Event handlers DOM directs

## Mobile First — Breakpoints
Ordre d'écriture Tailwind : base (375px) → `sm:` → `md:` → `lg:`
```tsx
// ✅
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:gap-6">
// ❌
<div className="flex flex-row gap-6">  // Casse sur mobile
```

## Transitions
```typescript
// Durée max : 200ms
// ✅
className="transition-all duration-200"
// ❌
className="transition-all duration-500"  // Trop lent, perçu comme laggy
```

## Couleurs Sémantiques Trajectoire
| Signal | Classe Tailwind |
|--------|----------------|
| Score ≥ 75 | `text-green-400` / `bg-green-500` |
| Score 50-74 | `text-yellow-400` / `bg-yellow-500` |
| Score < 50 | `text-red-400` / `bg-red-500` |
| Alerte critique | `border-red-700 bg-red-950` |
| Action principale | `bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-500` |
| Surface principale | `bg-gray-900 border-gray-700` |
| Background global | `bg-gray-950` |

## Chaque Bouton d'Action a un État Disabled
```tsx
<button
  onClick={handleSubmit}
  disabled={isLoading || !isValid}
  className="... disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
>
  {isLoading ? <Loader2 className="animate-spin" /> : "Analyser"}
</button>
```
